2296,"ok_print":true}],"intro":{"lead":"UNESCO Roman baths, Georgian architecture","body":"Bath is a historic Roman and Georgian spa city. It is famous for its hot springs, Roman period baths, Medieval heritage and stately Georgian architecture. Bath has been double UNESCO-listed as a World Heritage Site, both in its own right (in 1987) and as one of 11 \"Great Spa Towns of Europe\" (in 2021). Set in the rolling Somerset countryside on the southern edge of the Cotswolds, Bath (with a population around 90,000) offers a diverse range of attractions for its 4.4 million visitors each year: restaurants, theatres, cinemas, pubs and nightclubs, along with interesting museums, and a wide range of guided tours. It is also a university city.","grounding":[{"source":"wikivoyage","title":"Bath","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Bath","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"short":"Bath is a spa city in the United Kingdom, built in pale Georgian stone over Roman baths. Bath Abbey, the Royal Crescent and Pulteney Bridge are the set pieces, and ten hours covers them. June to September is the season.","short_src":"rewrite","facts":{"population":101557,"visit_h":7.3}},"highlights":[{"id":"hl-bath-abbey","name":"Bath Abbey","kind":"Church","lat":51.38139,"lon":-2.35889,"dist_km":0.0,"rank_score":10.9,"resolved_by":"catalogue"},{"id":"hl-pulteney-bridge","name":"Pulteney Bridge","kind":"Bridge","lat":51.38306,"lon":-2.35778,"dist_km":0.2,"rank_score":10.84,"resolved_by":"catalogue"},{"id":"hl-roman-baths","name":"Roman Baths","kind":"Museum","lat":51.3809,"lon":-2.3595,"dist_km":0.0,"rank_score":9.36,"resolved_by":"catalogue","image":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/08/Roman_Baths_in_Bath_Spa%2C_England_-_July_2006.jpg/960px-Roman_Baths_in_Bath_Spa%2C_England_-_July_2006.jpg","author":"Diliff","licence":"CC BY 2.5","licence_url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.5","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Roman_Baths_in_Bath_Spa,_England_-_July_2006.jpg","w":2638,"h":2296,"ok_print":true}}],"do":[{"name":"Roman Baths","type":"experience","detail":"Walk the torch-lit terraces of the 2000 year old bathing complex over the hot spring, rediscovered and rebuilt by the Victorians.","evidence":{"n_sources":11,"of":14,"urls":["https://visitbath.co.uk/things-to-do/","https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Bath","https://www.timeout.com/bath/things-to-do/best-things-to-do-in-bath"],"method":"web"},"sources":["web"]},{"name":"Thermae Bath Spa rooftop soak","type":"swim","detail":"Bathe in Britain's only naturally warm mineral waters, ending in the open-air rooftop pool with the Abbey and hills in view. Over 16s only.","link":"https://www.thermaebathspa.com/","evidence":{"n_sources":9,"of":14,"urls":["https://www.thermaebathspa.com/","https://visitbath.co.uk/things-to-do/","https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Bath"],"method":"web"},"sources":["web"]},{"name":"Royal Crescent and Circus stroll","type":"experience","detail":"Georgian set pieces a few lanes apart: the sweeping 30 house crescent above its lawn, the circle of townhouses, and No. 1 as a museum.","evidence":{"n_sources":9,"of":14,"urls":["https://visitbath.co.uk/things-to-do/","https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Bath","https://www.timeout.com/bath/things-to-do/best-things-to-do-in-bath"],"method":"web"},"sources":["web"]},{"name":"Bath Abbey and its tower tour","type":"activity","detail":"Fan-vaulted gothic abbey beside the springs; the guided tower climb looks straight down on the Roman Baths and across the city roofs.","evidence":{"n_sources":7,"of":14,"urls":["https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Bath","https://www.timeout.com/bath/things-to-do/best-things-to-do-in-bath","https://visitbath.co.uk/things-to-do/"],"method":"web"},"sources":["web"]},{"name":"River Avon boat trip and canal towpath","type":"activity","detail":"Cruise or row the Avon below Pulteney Bridge toward Bathampton, or follow the Kennet and Avon canal towpath out past Sydney Gardens.","season":[4,5,6,7,8,9,10],"e